  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two completed experiments (config_050, config_010) are nearly identical except for fusion (concat vs weighted), both using scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation, yielding ~0.72 accuracy. Weighted fusion is marginally better (0.7250 vs 0.7207). This gives us almost no information about whether the RNA encoder choice is a bottleneck. Question: config_038 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while keeping the best-performing fusion and aggregation. This tests whether a more biologically contextual RNA representation (scgpt) can push accuracy beyond the current ~0.72 plateau. Why this is the best next step: With only 2 data points and 7 experiments remaining, we must identify which axis (RNA encoder, image encoder, aggregation) offers the largest headroom. The image encoder (ViT-L) is already a very strong pretrained model, making the RNA encoder the most likely source of improvement. A positive result opens a new high-performing direction; a negative result confirms scvi_n200 is optimal and lets us focus remaining budget on other axes."
}

